**What the other forms do (the drafter read `backend/logSafe.js` and `backend/logger.js` at the sha; you re-read both whole at Step 2):** `logSafe.js:34` `function logSafe(value, max = DEFAULT_MAX)`, `:29` `DEFAULT_MAX = 500`; `:41` `s = s.replace(/\n|\r/g, '');` REMOVES every CR and LF (the empty replacement is the form CodeQL's barrier recognises, `:14`-`:21`); `:42` rewrites U+2028/U+2029 as visible escapes; `:43` rewrites other C0, DEL and C1 controls as `\xNN` (TAB kept); `:44` cuts past `max` with `…[+N chars]`. The two-argument form `logSafe(x, KQL_LOG_MAX_CHARS)` (the constant is `server.js:5982`, 2048) is no longer unprecedented: the five sinks of pull request 172 use it at `:6194`, `:6252`, `:6311` and alerts 174, 177 and 181 read `fixed` at `2026-11-06T04:30:41Z` on main's scan (the drafter's API read). `logger.js:241` `foldPrimitiveArgs` and `:260` the per-level wrapper fold every string, number, boolean, null and undefined argument after the message into the message with `String(arg)`, so a second argument that was a string stays a string and `logger.info('x:', query)` is the same line as `logger.info('x: ' + query)`; arrays are folded with `JSON.stringify`, objects stay meta. `console.log/error` has no such folding: a string prints raw, an object prints through `util.inspect` (which quotes and escapes CR/LF inside the object; a whole `req.body` at 214 and 217 therefore does NOT start a forged line at base, it PRINTS EVERY EXTRA FIELD'S VALUE, which is the red those two cells use).

