## LANDING (Tuesday's, quoted at source) AND WHAT A MERGE DOES
`/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md:2067`: "Merge path: open a PR from the gated branch, wait for CodeQL (a background wait that EXITS), then land the SAME commit. Never squash, never rebase ([[C-68]])." and `:2068`: "NEVER dismiss a code-scanning alert, from any side, and never touch the ruleset." The project's rule for Tuesday is a MERGE COMMIT with the head pinned to the gated sha (the repo allows all three methods: `gh api -X GET repos/datasecau/Reporting_Dashboard_Au` reads `allow_merge_commit` true, `allow_squash_merge` true, `allow_rebase_merge` true at 16:1x, so the choice is the rule's, not the repository's; C-68 at `:665`). C-190 ADDENDUM at `:2080`: "check BOTH thresholds before a PR. Security high+ AND any rule-severity `error` alert. `js/log-injection` counts, even when the interpolated value is a number derived from the request." You push a branch only.
**One PR, three commits, is the proposed lane.** The alerts are judged on main's analysis at the merge commit, after landing, never on the PR ref (a PR head reads fixed for every closed PR; that read cannot fail): the ticket moves on that, and a site CodeQL still reports after the merge is a new round on that site, not a re-read of this one. **Does a merge deploy anything? Read at source (`.github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml` at main `15b1426f`).** Trigger `:26`-`:28` `on: push: branches: [main]`, `:29`-`:32` `paths-ignore` `'**.md'`, `'docs/**'`, `'tests/**'` (the test folder here is `__tests__/`, which `tests/**` does not match, and `backend/server.js` is not ignored), plus `workflow_dispatch` `:33`. So **a merge of this branch to main DOES start a Deploy demo run**; what it does is set by `:53` (job `build`: `if: ${{ vars.CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED == 'true' && (...) }}`), `:91` (job `deploy`: `if: ${{ always() && vars.CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED == 'true' && (...) }}`) and `:95` (`environment: demo`). The drafter's reads at 16:1x: repository variables `total_count` 0 (so the switch is unset and both jobs skip); `environments` lists `dev` only; the run of the merge of pull request 172 itself (id `42162626357`, push, head `15b1426f`) is `completed` / `skipped` and its jobs `deploy` and `build` are both `skipped` (control: the same endpoint reports 4412 runs). **This seat never merges, never dispatches, never sets the variable, never deploys. Tuesday re-reads `vars.CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED` and the environment list immediately before the merge and reads the new run's two jobs after it; a merge must not deploy, and that read is how it is checked.**

